From 8f657f062688024b43b437d8a68c6434639344f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:46:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] perf(windows): remove 10ms poll from the remote bridge
 keystroke pump

The client->ssh pump polled PeekNamedPipe every 10ms because a blocking
named-pipe read cannot be unblocked from another thread, adding 0-10ms of
jitter to every keystroke (i0002 W4).

The pump now blocks in read; shutdown cancels the in-flight read with
CancelIoEx on the pipe handle (retried until the pump observes its stop
flag). CancelSynchronousIo does not work here: interprocess implements
'sync' named-pipe reads as internally-awaited overlapped I/O, invisible
to the synchronous cancel API - verified by a test that hung with it and
passes with CancelIoEx. The download pump is joined before cancelling, so
no other I/O on the pipe can be cancelled by accident.

Adds windows-sys Win32_System_IO for CancelIoEx and pump tests
(forward + close, cancel-while-blocked).
